             <property name="text">
              <string>Export</string>
             </property>
             <property name="toolTip">
              <string>Run the export: the enabled tasks first, then the enabled checks, then the write.
A failed check aborts before anything is written — but the tasks have already run, and the ones marked permanent stay applied.</string>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item>
            <widget class="QPushButton" name="b009">
             <property name="enabled">
              <bool>true</bool>
             </property>
             <property name="minimumSize">
              <size>
               <width>0</width>
               <height>18</height>
              </size>
             </property>
             <property name="maximumSize">
              <size>
               <width>16777215</width>
               <height>18</height>
              </size>
             </property>
             <property name="text">
              <string>Override Checks</string>
             </property>
             <property name="toolTip">
              <string>Skip every validation check and export regardless.
The tasks still run — this only disables the checks that would otherwise abort the write.
Use it to ship a known-imperfect asset on purpose, not as a way past a check you have not read.
It clears itself after a successful export, and never carries over to the next session.
You do not need it to retry: a run whose checks fail offers the same override in place, so the tasks are not re-run.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="checkable">
              <bool>true</bool>
             </property>
